// Title: Disabled Windows Defender Eventlog
// Sigma ID: fcddca7c-b9c0-4ddf-98da-e1e2d18b0157
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-04 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the disabling of the Windows Defender eventlog as seen in relation to Lockbit 3.0
//   infections
// False positives:
//   - Other Antivirus software installations could cause Windows to disable that eventlog (unknown)
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/WhichbufferArda/status/1543900539280293889/photo/2
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disabled_microsoft_defender_eventlog.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WINEVT\\Channels\\Microsoft-Windows-Windows Defender/Operational\\Enabled" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
